<html><head>

    <title>THIS pantry food clears out &quot;sticky blood&quot; caused by high blood sugar
    </title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <p dir="ltr">Scientists are reporting a disturbing discovery about why blood sugar causes so many complications...</p>

    <p dir="ltr">And it has nothing to do with your A1C numbers.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">Instead, it all comes down to something researchers are calling<strong> &quot;sticky blood&quot;...</strong></p>

    <p dir="ltr">A dangerous condition that develops when sugar stays in your bloodstream too long.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">[Think about what happens when you pour maple syrup down a thin straw...]</p>

    <p dir="ltr">That's exactly what's happening inside your blood vessels right now.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">What makes this particularly concerning is that most people have no idea it's happening...</p>

    <p dir="ltr">Until they're faced with serious complications.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">In fact, in just the last hour, sticky blood permanently disabled 17 Americans:</p>

    <p dir="ltr">- 10 lost limbs to amputation</p>
    <p dir="ltr">- 5 experienced kidney failure</p>
    <p dir="ltr">- 2 went blind</p>

    <p dir="ltr">But there's hope.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">A Texas doctor recently discovered that <strong><a href="http://aad.enia.net/cl/16_rd/1/0/985/592/6a7b6900e9e36f6ecff097fe">one common pantry food can help clear away this &quot;sticky blood&quot;...</a></strong></p>

    <p dir="ltr">Restoring healthy circulation throughout your body.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">In fact, in a study published in the American Journal of Clinical Nutrition, people who added more of this ONE food to their meals lowered their blood sugar so dramatically...</p>

    <p dir="ltr">They were able to reduce or eliminate their diabetes medication.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">Another study at Duke University showed similar results:</p>

    <p dir="ltr">7 out of 10 people who ate this food dropped their A1c and cut their medication in half.</p>

    <p dir="ltr">The craziest part?</p>

    <p dir="ltr">You probably have this blood sugar &quot;miracle&quot; sitting in your kitchen right now...</p>

    <p dir="ltr">But chances are, you've been told to AVOID it.</p>

    <p dir="ltr"><strong><a href="http://aad.enia.net/cl/16_rd/1/0/985/592/6a7b6900e9e36f6ecff097fe">==&gt; Watch this presentation to discover how to clear out &quot;sticky blood&quot;</a></strong></p>

    <p dir="ltr">- Jim</p>
